From: PS3 Custom Toolchain
Subject: [PATCH] cell64lv2: do not emit AIX traceback tables by default

The AIX traceback table (tbtab, .long 0 + .byte 0,<lang>,... at the end
of each function's .text) is emitted by rs6000-logue.cc:5290 when:
    (DEFAULT_ABI == ABI_AIX || DEFAULT_ABI == ABI_ELFv2)
     && ! flag_inhibit_size_directive
     && rs6000_traceback != traceback_none
     && !cfun->is_thunk

For the PS3 target the default ABI is AIX (set by the linux64 override),
and on Cell LV2 userspace the kernel never reads the AIX tbtab; the
backtrace walk is driven by .debug_frame / the CFA, not by the tbtab.
The table is 8+ bytes of dead weight per function.

rs6000.opt initialises rs6000_traceback to traceback_default (the
"unspecified by the user" sentinel); -mtraceback=full|part|no override it.
The override runs after option processing, so a plain assignment would
wipe out a user-specified -mtraceback. Gate the default on the sentinel:
set traceback_none only when rs6000_traceback is still traceback_default,
preserving an explicit -mtraceback.

Behaviour:
  default            no tbtab
  -mtraceback=full   tbtab
  -mtraceback=part   tbtab
  -mtraceback=no     no tbtab

--- a/gcc/config/rs6000/cell64lv2.h
+++ b/gcc/config/rs6000/cell64lv2.h
@@ -119,7 +119,11 @@
 /* Reuse the linux64-style override_options, identical to linux64.h.  */
 #undef	SUBSUBTARGET_OVERRIDE_OPTIONS
 #define	SUBSUBTARGET_OVERRIDE_OPTIONS				\
-  do rs6000_linux64_override_options (); while (0)
+  do { \
+       rs6000_linux64_override_options (); \
+       if (rs6000_traceback == traceback_default) \
+	 rs6000_traceback = traceback_none; \
+     } while (0)
 
